\n    (∀ m, D.embed (D.zM m) = D.z (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.z\\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LieLatticeData lam M\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0 : ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p : ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"D.H004\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"representation\":\"The arbitrary free lattice is M with a Z-basis and an injective inclusion into the complex highest-weight module V. The data record carries the actual complex operators and their integral restrictions. Scalar extension is represented by K tensor_Z M, with K acting on the first factor; this is related to the source ordering M tensor_Z K by the tensor commutor, which must be proved/used as a conversion. The target predicate means nonzero and every K-subspace invariant under all three induced actions is zero or the whole space. This is not a standard-lattice specialization.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\",\"S002\",\"S003\",\"S004\",\"S005\",\"S006\",\"S007\",\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"Single assembled obligation preserving the NL0 route: establish the divided-power basis and termination (S001), construct and preserve matrix units including the composite coefficient computation and p=2/lambda=0 cases (S002), analyze the arbitrary lattice coordinate modules and rank-one generator without presupposing freeness (S003), reduce via the arbitrary lattice basis to M tensor K and transport x,y,h (S004), show matrix units survive since r! and binomial coefficients are units for lambda<p (S005), extract a nonzero coordinate from a nonzero invariant subspace (S006), use E_{j,i} and invert the nonzero coordinate to obtain every basis vector (S007), and conclude nonzero irreducibility by the zero/nonzero case split (S008). This single node is intentionally a coarse source boundary; its implementation will need local elaboration into checked sublemmas without altering the given source assumptions.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T001\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T001\"}}}","status":"completed"}}

